  "interpretation": [
    "MLP has larger absolute branch discrepancy in each of3docs, but lower relative L2 because its reference branch amplitude is larger. This is not a contradiction.",
    "Both final branch outputs have4096channels and identical token counts, so their direct error-energy comparison is not inflated by dimension. Gate/Up/product internal14336channels require separate RMSE/referenceRMS; raw energy must not be ranked across those dimensions.",
    "AB includes different branch inputs and downstream amplification. It is not local arithmetic rounding loss.",
    "A/C shares decoder entrance. Attention entrance/input_norm is identical, while MLP entrance/post_attention_norm already differs. Therefore AC MLP is not same-MLP-entrance local error and cannot directly rank local Attention versus MLP rounding quality.",
    "For true same-MLP-entrance reference use R006 mlp_extension whole_mlp_local, not v5 checkpoint/BF16 record_mlp trace.",
    "CB preserves almost all AB branch discrepancy; together with A/C dynamics this supports inherited-input sensitivity, not a proven unique whole32layer source.",
    "MLP chain amplifies physical perturbations through shared dynamic A8 re-encoding and weighted transforms. A Down AB discrepancy includes its changed input; it must not be assigned to Down local rounding alone.",
    "No full1024 pure Attention comparison exists in current saved summaries; do not present the3doc branch table as1024 statistics."
